  "body": "## Request\n\nUsers and agents want to script CamCraft from Python (batch jobs, variants of a part, data from NumPy or SciPy), with typed calls instead of raw MCP messages.\n\n## Proposal (needs design)\n\nA Python package (for example `camcraft`) that starts `camcraft-cli mcp` and exposes each MCP tool as a typed Python function. Generate the functions from the schema listing (`camcraft-cli mcp --schemas`, see the schema issue), so the client stays in step with the tools.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Generated code in the repository, or generation at install time?\n- Version check between the package and the installed `camcraft-cli`.\n- Where the package lives (this repository or a separate one) and how it is released.\n\nDone means: a design decision in `docs/decisions/` and the sub-issues for the work.\n\nDepends on: the schema listing issue. Idea from SolidCraft 0.51 (Python client); our own implementation.\n",
